<% content_for :title, "AWSM Security" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "public-site" %>
<%= render "shared/public_header" %>
<main class="site-container trust-page">
  <header class="trust-page__header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Trust boundaries in plain language</p>
    <h1>The server coordinates. The client holds the keys.</h1>
    <p>AWSM separates <%= glossary_term_link "Account" %> authentication from <%= glossary_term_link "Vault" %> decryption so optional synchronization does not turn the server into a trusted Vault client.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose-stack">
    <section><h2>Account password</h2><p>The server receives the Account password over the protected connection and verifies it against a password digest. It identifies the Account for Host sessions and quotas. It cannot decrypt a Vault.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Public-page caching</h2><p>The landing, privacy, security, and glossary pages contain one anonymous representation with no Account data, CSRF token, or session cookie. A shared CDN may cache only those exact successful pages. Signed-in presentation is requested privately and is never shared-cache content.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Derived local-view boundary</h2><p>Derived local views are encrypted, rebuildable, and excluded from opaque Host items and Vault packages. AWSM does not currently ship a user-facing AI feature or a remote embedding-provider integration.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Recovery Phrase</h2><p>The 12-word <%= glossary_term_link "Recovery Phrase" %> remains client-held. A <%= glossary_term_link "Client Installation", "client installation" %> uses it to recover local <%= glossary_term_link "Vault" %> access and enroll a fresh <%= glossary_term_link "Client Credential" %>. AWSM cannot recover it for you.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Encrypted synchronization</h2><p><%= glossary_term_link "Zero-Knowledge Synchronization" %> means that a <%= glossary_term_link "Replica Host" %> stores opaque encrypted items and enforces its own protocol and operational rules. It does not interpret captured titles, page text, screenshots, or Vault keys.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Replica Access Grant and future protection</h2><p>Revoking a <%= glossary_term_link "Replica Access Grant" %> prevents future Host operations through that Grant. It cannot erase plaintext or keys already present in a <%= glossary_term_link "Client Installation", "client installation" %>. Vault authority changes and <%= glossary_term_link "Key Epoch" %> transitions remain client-held; AWSM does not promise remote wipe.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Replica availability</h2><p>Synchronization does not guarantee redundancy or remote retention. Keep the <%= glossary_term_link "Recovery Phrase" %> safe, and do not perform <%= glossary_term_link "Storage Relief", "storage relief" %> unless you understand the risk of losing items that no other <%= glossary_term_link "Replica" %> retains.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Technical detail</h2><p><%= link_to "Read the current security model", public_product_links[:security_model] %> for the formal trust assumptions and known boundaries.</p></section>
  </div>
</main>
<%= render "shared/public_footer" %>
